==Trivia==
*Although it sounds similar to ''loser'', the name Luza (ルーザ) is most likely derived from the Japanese word for monkey (猿 ''saru''), which becomes ''zaru'' in certain compound words due to ''[[wikipedia:Rendaku|rendaku]]''.
*Since it's a [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]], Great Ape Luza may have been inspired by ''Monster Hunter Rise: Sunbreak''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [[wikia:monsterhunter:Garangolm|Garangolm]], a huge, grey-and-green gorilla-like monster associated with nature. Despite trading the Behemoth type for [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]], its stronger variant [[Zero Luza]] shows further parallels to Garangolm, including heavily armored arms, eye color when attacking (red), and becoming more dangerous when its health drops below a certain threshold.
*Great Ape Luza's English description appears to have been mistranslated. It says that Luza itself can stand against Behemoths that wield the Ancient Curse, whereas the original Japanese description subtly suggests the use of units with [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayer]] and [[:Category:Cats with Curse Immunity|Curse Immunity]] (i.e., [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]], [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]], [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] and [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], which have both of these abilities and become available upon clearing [[Atonement for Sin]], the stage before Luza's debut).

